				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Charge It Up"
			x: -7.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["122843FE1BF8B653"]
			description: [
				"Fluix Crystals - charged certus + redstone + quartz dropped in water. The core material of every cable and device."
				""
				"&e&lThrow the ingredients into water as dropped items&r - this is an in-world transformation, not a crafting recipe. One charged certus, one redstone, one nether quartz, tossed into a water source block. They fuse after a moment."
				""
				"&e&lThen grow more instead of making more.&r Fluix crystals can be grown from seeds:"
				"&71.&r Craft &7Fluix Seeds&r from fluix dust."
				"&72.&r Drop them in water and wait, or speed it up with a &7Growth Accelerator&r."
				"&73.&r Harvest full crystals, crush some back into dust, repeat."
				""
				"&c&lThat loop is self-sustaining&r - it is the only reason AE2 is viable at scale. Set up a growth chamber early: a small water pool ringed with accelerators produces fluix and certus faster than you can spend it."
				""
				"&7Fluix goes into every cable, every processor, and every device in the mod. There is no such thing as too much.&r"
			]
			icon: "ae2:fluix_crystal"
			id: "06EEAC6C2BFD16FE"
			rewards: [{
				id: "344075EFB3D4B951"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 20
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Redstone, certus, quartz, water"
			tasks: [{
				id: "76038751ED078E6C"
				item: "ae2:fluix_crystal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Fluix Crystals"
			x: -5.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1FA9577AA6C0D787"]
			description: [
				"Silicon comes from the Inscriber. You'll need stacks of it for every processor."
				""
				"&e&lThe Inscriber has three slots and the layout matters:&r top press, bottom press, and a middle material slot. Presses are &lnot consumed&r - they stamp forever."
				""
				"&e&lThe four presses&r - Silicon, Logic, Calculation and Engineering - normally come from meteorites, which do not exist in a void world. &7SkyForge provides craftable press recipes&r so the whole mod is reachable. Make all four once and you never need them again."
				""
				"&e&lProcessor assembly is a three-step chain:&r"
				"&71.&r Inscribe silicon into a &7Printed Silicon&r."
				"&72.&r Inscribe the material (redstone/certus/gold) into its printed form."
				"&73.&r Combine printed silicon + printed material + redstone in the Inscriber to get the finished processor."
				""
				"&c&lAutomate this early.&r Processors are consumed by every AE2 device you will ever build, and hand-inscribing three stages per processor is genuinely miserable. A line of three Inscribers with pipes between them is one of the best hours you can spend."
				""
				"&8Remember the Inscriber itself is gated behind a Mekanism Advanced Control Circuit in this pack."
			]
			icon: "ae2:silicon"
			id: "714AA25143923BC8"
			rewards: [{
				id: "540653FF6C9ABF3F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 20
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Sky stone dust, pressed"
			tasks: [{
				id: "54DE9AD8EA3A1FB5"
				item: "ae2:silicon"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Silicon"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
